WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.690
<i>Wake up.</i>

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:07.980
<i>What is it?</i>

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.320
<i>Wake up, Waver Velvet!</i>

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:13.950
<i>Sir...</i>

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.820
<i>Kayneth!</i>

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:22.750
<i>So, are my lectures too ridiculous
for you to listen to?</i>

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:25.830
<i>That's not exactly the case.</i>

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:27.500
<i>Then, answer me this!</i>

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:31.420
<i>Why do you seek to enter
the Fifth Holy Grail War?</i>

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:35.300
<i>What do you seek with the Relic
you stole from me in hand,</i>

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.140
<i>and what do you desire?</i>

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.310
<i>I...</i>

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.770
<i>want to see him one more time!</i>

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.100
<i>A fool.</i>

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:46.850
<i>Servants are nothing more than minions.</i>

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:51.610
<i>Next time they materialize, someone like you
won't be remembered at all.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:57.160
<i>Even then... Even then,
I want to prove to him...</i>

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.580
<i>that I was the one who was inferior.</i>

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.370
<i>That he...</i>

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.660
<i>Rider was the hero
who should've been victorious!</i>

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:07.750
<i>Do you still think that way?</i>

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.920
<i>The Relic has been seized.</i>

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:15.420
<i>Hephaestion, who materialized, denied you
as a subject of the King of Conquerors.</i>

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:18.720
<i>Even then, you say you'll still fight?</i>

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:20.220
<i>Of course!</i>

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:22.470
<i>Answer me once more.</i>

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.890
<i>What do you think victory is for a Mage?</i>

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:30.520
<i>Being rid of all stereotypes
and simply arriving at the final destination.</i>

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:34.070
<i>Then, what is your final destination?</i>

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:38.070
<i>Answer me, Lord El-Melloi II!</i>

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:42.120
<i>I will answer you, my mentor!</i>

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:44.500
<i>What I need to seek right now...</i>

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:24.760
Why...

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.220
did you save me?

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:28.470
You were a warrior.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:34.150
Warriors should die in battlefields
whenever possible.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:37.820
So, you'll kill if it comes to battle again.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.570
That's right.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:45.240
You are somehow similar to me.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.040
I can tell when I look at that weapon.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:53.040
That must be a replica
of a Noble Phantasm of some great hero.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.790
And you, the wielder, also are.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.920
A living incarnation of a distant ideal.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:02.130
A counterfeit created for show.

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:05.300
Humans never change
no matter what era.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.430
However, though counterfeit,

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:12.520
you fight with your own desires.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.270
You and I...

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:15.770
are the same.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.820
My desires...

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.150
I don't know.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.700
You can't fight like that
without any desires for yourself.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.910
My current desire is...

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:31.950
with Sir...

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:34.460
But...

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:39.840
I see. You despise that narrow-minded scholar
to come out into the battlefield that much.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:45.050
Indeed. He will die
if he enters a Holy Grail War.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.140
He's not of a caliber to be victorious.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:50.390
But that is what he desires!

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.140
I want to grant him that wish!

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:56.350
Loyalty and glory
sometimes are contradictory.

00:04:57.190 --> 00:05:01.860
But if you can't overcome that contradiction,
both Master and Servant will perish.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.610
Master and Servant...

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.950
A king is like the Sun.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.280
Its heat burns away
anything that gets near.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:12.870
But subjects can't survive without the Sun.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:19.250
For you, was Iskandar, King of Conquerors,
someone of that nature?

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.130
Yes.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.880
There will be no other king like that.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:25.380
Even if he falls to illness,

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:30.140
he said he was going to go further
and see the Sea at the End of the World.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:34.140
A grand king drove us forward!

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:37.100
How heated all of his words were...

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.150
How much they glimmered...

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:44.530
I was his primary confidante.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:47.490
That's something I won't let anyone deny.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:49.370
But why were you...

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:54.790
Why were you alone reprimanding
Iskandar for his actions?

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:57.960
Ms. Hephaestion?

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.880
What did you see?

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.550
Answer me! What did you see?

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:06.220
In a dream,

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:07.800
you were asking,

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:11.600
"Is this what you desired?"

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:15.220
"Why didn't you let this go?"

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:18.140
You said, "Answer me, Iskandar!"

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.320
Oh, I should've known.

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:28.780
You're a Sibyl. It seems you're especially
versed in spiritual possession.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:33.990
Looks like it stopped snowing.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.750
When you can move again,
you can leave here.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.960
Though I don't know
if you can catch up to that train.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:48.260
I'm Mary Lil Fargo.

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:51.930
Can you talk to us about Trisha Fellows?

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.850
She's an old friend of mine.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:01.100
So, she has passed away.
I still can't believe it.

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:05.770
She was investigating a serial murder
that happened seven years ago.

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:08.740
Have you heard anything
about why she did so?

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.610
Olga Marie was abandoned.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.780
That's what Trisha said.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.700
Olga Marie is, um...

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:19.120
She's the daughter of Lord Animusphere!

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:24.000
It was about a month ago.
The last day that I met her...

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:31.130
<i>Seven years ago, Lord Animusphere
was researching about the Holy Grail War.</i>

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:32.510
<i>The Holy Grail War?</i>

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:35.970
<i>Yes. It was right around
when the serial murders were happening.</i>

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:39.640
<i>The Lord gained information
about the Holy Grail War from somewhere.</i>

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:42.850
<i>But it's a very minor Magecraft ritual
in the Far East, isn't it?</i>

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:44.440
<i>Why would you look into it
after all this time?</i>

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:47.320
<i>Since doing research
about the Holy Grail War,</i>

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:51.780
<i>after a while, the Lord stopped
showing interest in Olga Marie.</i>

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:55.660
<i>But a Mage not leaving anything
for his child can't be...</i>

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.200
<i>That Greater Grail was distorted,</i>

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:01.660
<i>and no matter what you do,
it can't grant the family's wish.</i>

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:03.500
<i>That's what the Lord said.</i>

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:07.590
<i>But what does that have to do
with him abandoning his daughter?</i>

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.420
<i>That's what I want to know.</i>

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:11.670
<i>What did the Lord find out
seven years ago?</i>

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:14.590
<i>How is it related
to the serial murder case?</i>

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:17.100
<i>And why did he abandon Olga Marie?</i>

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:21.810
Trisha was doing research
on the Holy Grail War,

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:24.400
and she boarded
the Mystic Eyes Collection Train.

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:26.940
The victims of the serial murders,

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:31.110
including Trisha herself, were wielders
of Mystic Eyes. Anything else?

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:33.150
A man without a heart.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:34.860
What's that about?

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.070
Someone with a nickname like that

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:42.000
was doing research on the Holy Grail War seven
years ago by request from Lord Animusphere.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:44.330
That's what she said.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:46.290
Thank you.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:48.420
This was of great help to us.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.630
Nothing less from the Rail Zeppelin!

00:08:55.630 --> 00:09:00.810
If it can locate a Leyline, not even
the Child of Einnashe will be an obstacle!

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:02.850
Is this a time to be celebrating?

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:06.230
I really do feel sorry about Gray!

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:09.610
But you know, she seems
like she can take a few hits!

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.690
Enough with the excuses.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:15.280
That's...

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:19.740
That hurts! It's cold!
I'm being shaven, planed, grated!

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:30.000
Wait, ouch, pain, ouch, pain,
I'm shaven, planed, grated, pain!

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:35.220
Open the door please!

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:38.680
And there we go!

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:39.890
Made it in time!

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.560
I'm so glad!

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:44.140
Oh, this is so amusing!

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:46.560
It definitely was worth
crashing a helicopter for!

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:49.480
Mr. Caules, how is Sir doing?

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:50.730
He's fine.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.900
His condition stabilized
soon after leaving that forest.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:55.490
I see.

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:59.070
What, weak in the knees?

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:01.990
And harsh treatment aside,
you didn't have to ride on the shield!

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:03.160
Enough already!

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:06.330
You should be more mannered
in how you treat a box—

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:10.040
Gray! Stop! Hey! Stop! Gray! Hey!

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:12.170
Hey, what's wrong, Missie?

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:15.170
You suddenly have
a sour look on your face.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:17.420
A man without a heart.

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:23.100
I've heard rumors of a dangerous Mage
who once had his heart stolen by a Fairy.

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:24.430
By a Fairy?

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:28.890
If he's the person I know of,
he has a younger sister-in-law.

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:32.650
And she's currently aboard that train.

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:34.860
Hey, that can't be!

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:36.150
No way!

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:40.610
I'm having everyone gather up
in the lobby car.

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.490
Since the usual individual
is still sleeping slovenly,

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:48.910
I will play detective for now.

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:51.920
Lord El-Melloi II's Case Files
｛Rail Zeppelin｝Grace note

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:57.720
What in the world is the reason
you want all of us?

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:04.260
There's something I'd like to suggest
from the standpoint of the Policies division.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:07.640
Right, it's about the perpetrator of this case.

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:09.640
Oh yeah, Great Detective!

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:15.110
There was a serial murder case that used
the same method seven years ago.

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:20.110
Pardon me, but I don't recollect
any cases of that nature.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:24.030
We at Policies had controlled
information about it.

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:26.330
Wow, you'd actually admit that?

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:29.870
However, we weren't the only ones
who meddled in this.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:32.880
The Holy Church had also intervened.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:38.550
The investigator in charge at the time
was you, Karabo Frampton, right?

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:40.130
Correct.

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:42.680
Come on now! If you knew about it,
you could say so!

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:45.550
That goes against my duties
of confidentiality. Naturally.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:46.850
I see.

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.980
Even with Mr. Karabo's Past Vision,

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:52.440
the crime scene couldn't be viewed.

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:57.230
Even with Ms. Trisha's Premonition,
she couldn't protect her own self.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:58.730
I see.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:02.360
So, the instant of the crime couldn't be viewed
either from the past or the future.

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:06.160
That would leave us
with one answer, plain and simple.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:09.540
That location wasn't the scene of the crime.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:13.370
I see! I get it! But of course!

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:16.210
As I'd expect from a Mystic Eyes specialist...

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:20.550
Past Vision and Premonition
only transcend over the temporal axis.

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:23.590
If so, if you're not
at the scene of the crime,

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:25.930
you can't see visions
no matter how hard you try.

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:29.060
The crime scene wasn't that room?

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:33.640
Then, who are you saying
murdered Ms. Trisha?

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:38.520
Now, I'll have one witness
enter the stage.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.250
What is the meaning of this?

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:55.620
Her head was hidden
using Imaginary Magecraft.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:00.130
I presume that Trisha Fellows herself
had sealed it away.

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:02.630
She sealed away her own head?

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:07.890
She likely realized she was going to die
by beheading thanks to her Premonition.

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:13.140
She'd created an Imaginary pocket in advance
to where the head would likely fall.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:15.850
And this is the important part.

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:18.400
Inside a spell of Imaginary Magecraft,

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:20.150
time stands still.

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:24.650
Therefore, her head at the time
of retrieval was still alive.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.950
It was still alive?

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:32.790
With the final breath left in her throat,
she uttered just one word.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.710
What do you think
was the word she left behind?

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:39.210
<i>"Karabo."</i>

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.550
Karabo Frampton,

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.970
your Mystic Eyes are those
of Observation of Past Vision, correct?

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:49.010
What is Observation of Past Vision?

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:51.890
They're Mystic Eyes
that can see a commonplace past.

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:54.680
You can perceive a past
that's already been settled.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:58.690
Even if you can see the past,
you can't commit a murder, right?

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.310
Well, right.

00:14:00.610 --> 00:14:02.440
Among powerful Mystic Eyes,

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:06.700
there are those who can bring
the visions into the world as truth.

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:09.370
For instance,
"The Mystic Eyes of Death Perception."

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:10.740
The legendary?

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:13.410
But those are Rainbow-class
or Jewel-class!

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:15.540
Of course, this is only
if the rumors are true.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:20.670
But your Mystic Eyes are rather close
to that, aren't they, Father Karabo?

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:32.180
I will record a slash like this
and put it aside.

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:36.180
Then, if the wielder
of the Mystic Eyes had observed it,

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:40.690
the target will be severed
in the exact manner of the recorded slash.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:45.440
I see.

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.400
So, didn't you do it?

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:52.120
Didn't you do it, Karabo Frampton?

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:55.040
You're saying I did it?

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:59.790
A train following the rails worked in your favor.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:03.790
You just took a slice of empty air
in the lobby car leading the way.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:10.220
It'd be easy to see what location
the chair would be with your Past Vision.

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:12.680
Because when her corpse was found,

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:16.600
the train had stopped in the woods,
and you were outside.

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:20.980
You simply needed to peek
into the window from the outside.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:24.730
Then, dragged into the past you observed,

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:27.070
empty air would be torn apart once again...

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:31.030
right along with Trisha Fellows' head.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:38.700
Wait? Does that mean the serial murder
from seven years ago was also like this?

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:43.540
I can't think there would be anyone else
with Mystic Eyes like that!

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:47.500
And that individual was involved
in the investigation, huh?

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:48.670
Hold on, I...

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:52.090
I won't conclude
that you're the perpetrator,

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:55.930
but this gives enough reason
to take certain measures against you.

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:57.470
Wait a minute!

00:15:59.100 --> 00:15:59.980
Oh?

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:04.100
Are you finally awake, Lord El-Melloi II?

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:05.520
Waver!

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:08.860
I didn't think
you'd be here, as well, Melvin.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:12.700
Oh! It's only natural for me to rush over
when my best friend's in peril!

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.070
Just mind your own business.

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:15.950
Ms. Adashino...

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:18.830
I have several doubts
on your deduction.

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:24.000
You're already going to let me in
on your marvelous detective work?

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:28.630
The deduction you just mentioned is lacking
the element of motive to begin with.

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:31.050
"Whydunit," your favorite?

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:34.050
Correct. No crime exists
without a motive.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:37.560
If you really need a reason,

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:40.390
how about envisioning
you and the bloodthirsty killer

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:42.690
as one and the same
with Mystic Eyes of Past Vision?

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:43.640
What?

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:46.480
As he kept observing
the murders seven years ago,

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:49.530
the sense of self and the killer
melded together.

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:53.030
Wouldn't that be possible
if he no longer can control his Mystic Eyes?

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.660
Are you seriously saying that?

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:56.370
Would it be okay if I was serious?

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:59.700
There isn't much of a difference
between serious and nonsensical.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.870
After all, we are Mages.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:04.000
So, that's your scenario.

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:08.790
But does Father Karabo's Mystic Eyes
really have that kind of power?

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:10.710
What do you mean by that?

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:17.640
Who proved that his Mystic Eyes could
bring forth a recorded vision of the past?

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:20.640
Are you saying that is nothing
more than my deduction?

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:24.640
It's not even worth calling it a presumption
or even circumstantial evidence.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.520
To be blunt, it's just a delusion.

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:29.900
Are you going to prosecute him
based on something like that?

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:32.610
You don't need to worry about that at all.

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:36.990
All we need to do is to have
the Mystic Eyes appraised by Rail Zeppelin.

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:39.410
Yes. It would be possible
with those Mystic Eyes.

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:47.250
Indeed, it can project a slash
lost in the past back into the present.

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:51.960
Everyone, this is
the deputy manager of this train.

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:54.130
It is now the appointed time.

00:17:54.130 --> 00:17:57.180
I'm here to take your Mystic Eyes
before the auction.

00:17:57.550 --> 00:17:59.180
Appointed time?

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:01.850
The staff should've told you already...

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:06.140
that we'll be extracting your Mystic Eyes
half a day before the auction.

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:09.440
I see, so you thought
this would be the perfect timing

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:12.530
for Rail Zeppelin to back up
your deductions!

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:14.530
You are perceptive.

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:18.320
B-But wait!

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:19.570
Not yet!

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:31.170
Deputy Manager...

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:43.180
This is marvelous!

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:47.560
It falls short of Rainbow-class,
but it'll likely reach at least Jewel-class.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:48.940
Then, it really does?

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:54.440
A past shadow long gone can be
brought back to the present like sea-foam.

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:57.570
Shall we name it
"Mystic Eyes of Transience"?

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:03.030
I do apologize wholeheartedly
for taking all of your precious time.

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:09.210
I hope you'll be able to resume
a pleasant journey aboard Rail Zeppelin.

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:21.140
So, why are you tagging along?

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:24.350
Of course I'd tag along!
I'm your best friend!

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:28.140
I'll cry if you keep being so cold to me!
I'll cough blood!

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:34.480
Do you really think Mr. Karabo
was the one who killed Ms. Trisha?

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:38.650
There's a large difference
between possibility and actual execution.

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:47.790
I'm terribly sorry.
We're keeping you restrained for now.

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:48.830
Of course.

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:50.830
I'd like to ask you...

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:55.090
Were you really involved
in a serial murder seven years ago?

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:57.920
I don't know.

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:04.510
I honestly had forgotten until just moments ago
that I was involved in that incident.

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:06.760
The effects of your Mystic Eyes.

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:08.390
I can see the past.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:10.480
It's forced on me
even if I don't want to see.

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:12.600
Whether my eyes are open or shut,

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:16.400
the images flood in as if laughing
at me that my eyelids don't matter.

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:21.740
However, at a greater pace than that,
my own memories become shattered.

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:23.780
That's the kind of Mystic Eyes they were.

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:28.040
In other words, you were completely
unable to control those Mystic Eyes.

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.120
I guess so.

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:34.630
But now, if I had those Mystic Eyes...

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:40.550
If I had them, I might finally
be able to unravel the truth!

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:43.760
Then, you can buy the Mystic Eyes
back in the auction!

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:47.470
Perhaps, but it won't be a sum
I can successfully make a winning bid.

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:50.220
I see. So, you just want to buy it back?

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:51.600
Melvin...

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:55.400
I can't guarantee it because I'm sure it'll be
the most expensive item this time around.

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:57.940
But it might be fun
to at least challenge myself.

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:01.990
Of course, it's only if it has
that much amusement attached to it.

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:03.450
What do you think, Waver?

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:05.870
I have no intent on selling
my soul to the devil.

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:06.990
A shame...

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:11.540
Isn't there something to make
this case a bit more exciting?

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:14.290
By the way, when I met Ms. Trisha...

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:17.590
Um...

00:21:17.840 --> 00:21:21.050
Tucked in her clothes was, well, um...

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:22.670
something lewd.

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:23.840
What was that?

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:26.090
Tell me again! What did you see?

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:27.760
Um...

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:31.640
I saw a man and a woman
connected together—

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:34.600
It's not strange to bring something in.

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:37.480
I myself had taken
several defensive measures.

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:40.820
But nothing like that
was at the crime scene.

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:42.940
Even if it was a defensive measure,

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:45.740
it's nowhere nearly as stable
as a Mystic Eyes nullifier.

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:50.990
So, that means she had
a different way to use it.

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:52.450
Sir?

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:55.000
This is not a deduction.
I can't possibly call this a deduction.

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:56.210
However,

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:58.830
if what I imagine is true, I can say this...

00:21:59.290 --> 00:22:00.710
The perpetrator is...

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:02.840
my enemy!

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:06.930
I will solve...

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:09.930
EPISODE 10: Rail Zeppelin 4/6
Mystic Eyes of Transience
and an Awakening Detective

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:09.930
this case!
